        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "653bcd9c-66f7-5f12-923e-09b48db3dfd1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Howea, H. forsteriana, Bulbophyllum, Linospadicinae, Linospadix\n- Places: Northern Hemisphere, Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, West Indies, Indian Ocean, Pacific Ocean\n- Topics: indoor plants, palm seed industry, newly germinated seedlings, plant distribution, palm taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- H. forsteriana is commonly grown as an indoor plant in the Northern Hemisphere.\n- The two Howea species form the mainstay of the island's palm seed industry.\n- The two Howea species are more importantly central to the island's trade in newly germinated seedlings.\n- Bulbophyllum is found throughout most of the warmer parts of the world, including Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, the West Indies, and various islands in the Indian and Pacific Oceans.\n- Linospadicinae is a subtribe of palm trees.\n- Linospadicinae includes the genera Howea and Linospadix.",
